# The ledger of `tracing`: what OpenTelemetry's SDKs for Go, Python and Rust
# let a program do with spans, their context and log records, one block per
# capability, and what Rebel answers. None of the three standard libraries
# traces, so the yardstick is the census the author chose on 2026-11-17,
# measured on this machine on 2026-11-18: Go's `go.opentelemetry.io/otel`
# 1.47.0 (`otel`, `trace`, `propagation`, `baggage`, `codes`, `attribute`,
# `sdk/trace`, `sdk/resource`, `log`, `sdk/log`,
# `exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp`,
# `exporters/otlp/otlplog/otlploghttp` 0.23.0; `go doc -all`, the modules
# fetched into the scratch folder); Python's `opentelemetry-api` and
# `opentelemetry-sdk` 1.45.2 and `opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-proto-http`
# (`dir()`, installed into the scratch folder); Rust's `opentelemetry`,
# `opentelemetry_sdk` and `opentelemetry-otlp` 0.33 (their rustdoc, built into
# the scratch folder).
#
# Behaviour was asked of Go's and Python's propagators on 18 `traceparent`
# fields and 29 `tracestate` fields, of Go's ratio sampler on eight trace ids
# at five ratios, of Python's exporter for the span flags and status it
# writes, and of `opentelemetry-proto` 1.45 for the bytes of a spans request
# and a logs request. Where they disagree, the note says whose answer was
# taken and why.

capability context/ids  a trace's and a span's ids, valid or not, read and written as hexadecimal
  heroes  tracing.SpanContext, tracing.is_valid, tracing.parse_trace_id, tracing.parse_span_id, tracing.format_id
  go      trace.TraceID, TraceID.IsValid, TraceID.String, TraceID.MarshalJSON, TraceIDFromHex, trace.SpanID, SpanID.IsValid, SpanID.String, SpanID.MarshalJSON, SpanIDFromHex, trace.SpanContext, NewSpanContext, SpanContextConfig, SpanContext.IsValid, HasTraceID, HasSpanID, TraceID, SpanID, IsRemote, Equal, WithTraceID, WithSpanID, WithRemote, MarshalJSON
  rust    opentelemetry::TraceId, SpanId, trace::SpanContext
  python  trace.SpanContext, SpanContext.is_valid, trace_id, span_id, is_remote, format_trace_id, format_span_id, INVALID_TRACE_ID, INVALID_SPAN_ID, INVALID_SPAN_CONTEXT
  note    A context is a record built directly, so Go's `With` copies are a field set on a copy

capability context/flags  the trace flags: sampled, and random as W3C level 2 names it
  heroes  tracing.is_sampled, tracing.FLAG_SAMPLED, tracing.FLAG_RANDOM
  go      trace.TraceFlags, FlagsSampled, FlagsRandom, TraceFlags.IsSampled, IsRandom, WithSampled, WithRandom, String, MarshalJSON, SpanContext.TraceFlags, SpanContext.IsSampled, SpanContext.IsRandom, SpanContext.WithTraceFlags
  rust    opentelemetry::TraceFlags
  python  trace.TraceFlags, DEFAULT_TRACE_OPTIONS, SpanContext.trace_flags

capability context/ids-generated  new ids drawn at random, never all zeros
  heroes  tracing.new_tracer, tracing.Tracer
  go      sdk/trace.IDGenerator, WithIDGenerator
  rust    opentelemetry_sdk::trace::IdGenerator, RandomIdGenerator
  python  sdk.trace.IdGenerator, RandomIdGenerator, id_generator
  note    A tracer's `generator`, seeded by the system's generator; a test sets one of its own, as a custom generator is set in Go and Python

capability propagation/traceparent  the `traceparent` field read and written
  heroes  tracing.parse_traceparent, tracing.format_traceparent
  go      propagation.TraceContext, TraceContext.Extract, TraceContext.Inject, TraceContext.Fields
  rust    opentelemetry_sdk::propagation::TraceContextPropagator
  python  trace.propagation.tracecontext.TraceContextTextMapPropagator
  note    Go and Python agree on 15 of 18 fields asked; where they differ: flags of `ff` are kept, as Python keeps them (Go refuses a byte above 3, while the Recommendation asks that unknown flags be ignored, not refused); a space before or after the field is refused, as Go refuses it (Python trims, and `http` has already trimmed a field's value). A version after `00` may go on after a `-`, and a version `00` field may not, as both read it

capability propagation/tracestate  the `tracestate` field read, written and changed by a vendor
  heroes  tracing.parse_tracestate, tracing.format_tracestate, tracing.with_state, tracing.without_state, tracing.state_of, tracing.StateMember
  go      trace.TraceState, ParseTraceState, TraceState.Insert, Delete, Get, Len, Walk, String, MarshalJSON, SpanContext.TraceState, SpanContext.WithTraceState
  rust    opentelemetry::trace::TraceState
  python  trace.TraceState, DEFAULT_TRACE_STATE, SpanContext.trace_state
  note    Go and Python agree on every field asked: a member that breaks the rules, a key twice or 33 members drops the whole field and keeps the context; spaces around a member and empty members are passed over

capability propagation/http  a context read from a request's fields and written into them
  heroes  tracing.extract, tracing.inject
  go      propagation.TextMapPropagator, TextMapCarrier, HeaderCarrier, HeaderCarrier.Get, Set, Keys, Values, MapCarrier, MapCarrier.Get, Set, Keys, ValuesGetter, NewCompositeTextMapPropagator, otel.GetTextMapPropagator, otel.SetTextMapPropagator
  rust    opentelemetry::propagation::Extractor, Injector, TextMapPropagator, FieldIter, TextMapCompositePropagator, global::get_text_map_propagator, global::set_text_map_propagator, trace::noop::NoopTextMapPropagator
  python  propagate.extract, propagate.inject, propagate.get_global_textmap, propagate.set_global_textmap, propagate.composite, textmap, OTEL_PROPAGATORS
  note    The fields are `http`'s `Header` list, so no carrier is needed; there is one propagator, W3C's, and no global to set

capability propagation/baggage  W3C baggage: key and value pairs carried with a request
  heroes  pending
  go      baggage.Baggage, baggage.New, Parse, Member, NewMember, NewMemberRaw, Property, NewKeyProperty, NewKeyValueProperty, NewKeyValuePropertyRaw, Baggage.Member, Members, SetMember, DeleteMember, Len, String, ContextWithBaggage, ContextWithoutBaggage, FromContext, propagation.Baggage, Baggage.Extract, Baggage.Inject, Baggage.Fields
  rust    opentelemetry::baggage::Baggage, BaggageExt, BaggageMetadata, KeyValueMetadata, Iter, opentelemetry_sdk::propagation::BaggagePropagator
  python  baggage.get_all, get_baggage, set_baggage, remove_baggage, clear, baggage.propagation.W3CBaggagePropagator
  note    Not written yet: the `baggage` field's grammar is its own

capability sampling  which traces are recorded: always, never, by a ratio of the trace id, or as the parent was
  heroes  tracing.Sampler, tracing.samples_root, tracing.samples_child
  go      sdk/trace.Sampler, AlwaysSample, NeverSample, TraceIDRatioBased, ParentBased, SamplingParameters, SamplingResult, SamplingDecision, Drop, RecordAndSample
  rust    opentelemetry_sdk::trace::Sampler, ShouldSample, SamplingDecision, SamplingResult, ParentBasedSampler
  python  sdk.trace.sampling.Sampler, ALWAYS_ON, ALWAYS_OFF, DEFAULT_ON, DEFAULT_OFF, TraceIdRatioBased, ParentBased, ParentBasedTraceIdRatio, StaticSampler, Decision, SamplingResult, OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER, OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG
  note    The ratio is Go's, held to its decisions on eight ids at five ratios: the last 8 bytes of the id, the lowest bit dropped, below the ratio times 2^63. Python compares all 64 bits with the ratio times 2^64, which differs at the edge of one id in 2^64

capability sampling/parent-cases  a parent-based sampler with its own choice for each kind of parent
  heroes  pending
  go      ParentBasedSamplerOption, WithLocalParentNotSampled, WithLocalParentSampled, WithRemoteParentNotSampled, WithRemoteParentSampled
  rust    -
  python  ParentBased(remote_parent_sampled=, remote_parent_not_sampled=, local_parent_sampled=, local_parent_not_sampled=)
  note    `parent_or_ratio` is OpenTelemetry's default of the four, the parent's decision kept

capability sampling/record-only  a span recorded and not exported
  heroes  pending
  go      AlwaysRecord, RecordOnly
  rust    SamplingDecision::RecordOnly
  python  AlwaysRecordSampler, Decision.RECORD_ONLY
  note    A span is a value the program holds, recorded or not; only one sampled is kept by `end`

capability tracer/provider  a tracer with its resource, scope, sampler, limits and clock
  heroes  tracing.new_tracer, tracing.with_sampler, tracing.with_resource, tracing.with_scope, tracing.with_limits, tracing.with_clock, tracing.Scope
  go      sdk/trace.TracerProvider, NewTracerProvider, TracerProvider.Tracer, TracerProviderOption, WithSampler, WithResource, WithSpanLimits, WithRawSpanLimits, WithAttributeValueDepthLimit, trace.Tracer, TracerProvider, TracerConfig, NewTracerConfig, TracerOption, WithInstrumentationVersion, WithInstrumentationAttributes, WithInstrumentationAttributeSet, WithSchemaURL
