  python  sdk.trace.TracerProvider, TracerProvider.get_tracer, Tracer, InstrumentationScope, InstrumentationInfo
  note    One tracer holds what a provider and its tracers hold apart; a scope's attributes and schema URL are not written

capability tracer/global  a tracer set once for the whole program
  heroes  refused: the language has no globals; the program passes its tracer `@`
  go      otel.Tracer, otel.GetTracerProvider, otel.SetTracerProvider, trace.NewNoopTracerProvider
  rust    opentelemetry::global::tracer, tracer_provider, tracer_with_scope, set_tracer_provider, BoxedTracer, BoxedSpan, GlobalTracerProvider, ObjectSafeTracer, ObjectSafeTracerProvider, ObjectSafeSpan
  python  trace.get_tracer, get_tracer_provider, set_tracer_provider, ProxyTracer, ProxyTracerProvider, OTEL_PYTHON_TRACER_PROVIDER

capability spans/start  a root span, and a span under a parent's context
  heroes  tracing.start, tracing.start_child, tracing.Span, tracing.SpanKind
  go      trace.Tracer.Start, SpanStartOption, WithSpanKind, WithNewRoot, WithLinks, WithAttributes, WithTimestamp, SpanConfig, NewSpanStartConfig, trace.SpanKind, ValidateSpanKind, SpanKind.String
  rust    opentelemetry::trace::Tracer::start, start_with_context, build, SpanBuilder, SpanKind
  python  Tracer.start_span, trace.SpanKind
  note    A parent that is not valid starts a root, as Go does; the new span keeps the parent's flags but sampled, and its state

capability spans/current  the span current in a context passed through calls
  heroes  refused: no context is passed in secret and nothing is global; the program passes the span, or its `context`, to the code under it, and `start_child` names it
  go      trace.ContextWithSpan, SpanFromContext, ContextWithSpanContext, ContextWithRemoteSpanContext, SpanContextFromContext, LinkFromContext
  rust    opentelemetry::context::Context, ContextGuard, FutureExt, WithContext, trace::TraceContextExt, get_active_span, mark_span_as_active, FutureExt, WithContext, SpanRef
  python  trace.get_current_span, set_span_in_context, use_span, Tracer.start_as_current_span, context

capability spans/attributes  a span's attributes, a key set again replacing it
  heroes  tracing.set_attribute, tracing.Attribute, tracing.AttributeValue
  go      trace.Span.SetAttributes, attribute.KeyValue, attribute.Key, attribute.Value, attribute.String, Int, Int64, Float64, Bool, StringSlice, Int64Slice, Float64Slice, BoolSlice, attribute.Set, NewSet, Distinct, Filter, Iterator, Sortable
  rust    opentelemetry::KeyValue, Key, Value, Array, StringValue, trace::Span::set_attribute, set_attributes
  python  Span.set_attribute, Span.set_attributes, util.types.Attributes, BoundedAttributes
  note    A list of texts is the one list kept, the others written as texts by the program; an attribute set is a list the program holds

capability spans/events  an event at a moment, and an error recorded as the event `exception`
  heroes  tracing.add_event, tracing.record_error, tracing.Event
  go      trace.Span.AddEvent, RecordError, EventOption, EventConfig, NewEventConfig, SpanEventOption, SpanStartEventOption, SpanEndEventOption, WithStackTrace, sdk/trace.Event
  rust    opentelemetry::trace::Span::add_event, add_event_with_timestamp, record_error, Event
  python  Span.add_event, Span.record_exception, sdk.trace.Event, EventBase, EXCEPTION_MESSAGE, EXCEPTION_TYPE, EXCEPTION_STACKTRACE, EXCEPTION_ESCAPED
  note    `exception.message` alone: no stack is read, and a failure has a code, not a type

capability spans/links  a link to another span's context
  heroes  tracing.add_link, tracing.Link
  go      trace.Link, Span.AddLink, sdk/trace.Link
  rust    opentelemetry::trace::Link, Span::add_link
  python  trace.Link, Span.add_link

capability spans/status  a span's status: unset, ok, or an error with its message
  heroes  tracing.set_status, tracing.Status, tracing.StatusCode
  go      trace.Span.SetStatus, codes.Code, codes.Unset, codes.Error, codes.Ok, Code.String, Code.MarshalJSON, Code.UnmarshalJSON, sdk/trace.Status
  rust    opentelemetry::trace::Status, Span::set_status
  python  trace.Status, StatusCode, Span.set_status
  note    OpenTelemetry's rules: `ok` is final, `unset` never replaces another, a message is kept for `error` alone

capability spans/name-and-end  a span renamed, and ended at the clock's moment
  heroes  tracing.rename, tracing.end
  go      trace.Span.SetName, Span.End, SpanEndOption, NewSpanEndConfig, Span.IsRecording, Span.SpanContext, Span.TracerProvider
  rust    opentelemetry::trace::Span::update_name, end, end_with_timestamp, is_recording, span_context
  python  Span.update_name, Span.end, Span.is_recording, Span.get_span_context
  note    The end's moment is the tracer's clock, which a test fixes with `with_clock`

capability spans/limits  how many attributes, events and links a span keeps, and how long a text
  heroes  tracing.Limits, tracing.default_limits, tracing.with_limits
  go      sdk/trace.SpanLimits, NewSpanLimits
