  note    128 of each by default, as the three SDKs; a text is cut where it is exported, so the span keeps what the program set

capability spans/http-server  a server's span from a request, with OpenTelemetry's HTTP conventions
  heroes  tracing.start_server, tracing.set_response
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    What Go's `otelhttp` and Python's instrumentations of the contrib repositories do, which the census did not reach: the caller's `traceparent` read, `http.request.method`, `url.path`, `url.query`, `user_agent.original`, `client.address`, `http.response.status_code`, and an error for 500 and above

capability export/otlp-http  spans posted to a collector by OTLP over HTTP, with retries and the environment's settings
  heroes  tracing.encode_spans, tracing.export_spans, tracing.otlp_to, tracing.otlp_from_env, tracing.Otlp, tracing.Exported, tracing.Signal, tracing.TRACES_URL
  go      otlptracehttp.New, NewClient, NewUnstarted, Option, WithEndpoint, WithEndpointURL, WithURLPath, WithHeaders, WithCompression, Compression, WithEncoding, Encoding, WithRetry, RetryConfig, WithTimeout, WithInsecure, WithTLSClientConfig, WithProxy, HTTPTransportProxyFunc, WithHTTPClient, WithMaxRequestSize, WithMaxResponseSize, sdk/trace.SpanExporter, ReadOnlySpan, ReadWriteSpan
  rust    opentelemetry_otlp::SpanExporter, SpanExporterBuilder, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_HEADERS, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_COMPRESSION, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_TIMEOUT, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_PROTOCOL, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_INSECURE, opentelemetry_sdk::trace::SpanData, SpanExporter, error::ExportError, OTelSdkError, OTelSdkResult
  python  trace_exporter.OTLPSpanExporter, DEFAULT_ENDPOINT, DEFAULT_TRACES_EXPORT_PATH, DEFAULT_TIMEOUT, DEFAULT_COMPRESSION, Compression, encode_spans, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_HEADERS, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_COMPRESSION, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_TIMEOUT, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_CERTIFICATE, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_CLIENT_CERTIFICATE, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_CLIENT_KEY, SpanExportResult, ReadableSpan, RequestPayloadTooLargeError
  note    Held byte for byte to `opentelemetry-proto` 1.45's serialization of a server's span under a remote parent and a root: a span's `flags` say only whether its parent was remote, 256 or 768, and its status is always written, as Python's exporter fills them

capability export/batch  ended spans queued and sent in batches
  heroes  tracing.end, tracing.export_spans, tracing.Limits
  go      sdk/trace.NewBatchSpanProcessor, BatchSpanProcessorOption, BatchSpanProcessorOptions, WithBatcher, WithMaxQueueSize, WithMaxExportBatchSize, WithBatchTimeout, WithExportTimeout, WithBlocking, TracerProvider.ForceFlush, TracerProvider.Shutdown
  rust    opentelemetry_sdk::trace::BatchSpanProcessor, BatchSpanProcessorBuilder, BatchConfig, BatchConfigBuilder, OTEL_BSP_EXPORT_TIMEOUT, OTEL_BSP_EXPORT_TIMEOUT_DEFAULT, OTEL_BSP_MAX_EXPORT_BATCH_SIZE, OTEL_BSP_MAX_EXPORT_BATCH_SIZE_DEFAULT, OTEL_BSP_MAX_QUEUE_SIZE, OTEL_BSP_MAX_QUEUE_SIZE_DEFAULT, OTEL_BSP_SCHEDULE_DELAY, OTEL_BSP_SCHEDULE_DELAY_DEFAULT
  python  sdk.trace.export.BatchSpanProcessor, BatchProcessor, OTEL_BSP_EXPORT_TIMEOUT, OTEL_BSP_MAX_EXPORT_BATCH_SIZE, OTEL_BSP_MAX_QUEUE_SIZE, OTEL_BSP_SCHEDULE_DELAY
  note    The queue is the tracer's `ended`, 2048 by default, a span past it dropped and counted; 512 a request, as the SDKs default to. No timer: the program calls `export_spans` when it chooses, there being no thread that shares the tracer

